# ---------------------------------
#   boxes pre-started at login
# ---------------------------------
#
# One DESKTOP-ENTRY ID per line — the file name under
# ~/.local/share/applications or /usr/share/applications, without the
# `.desktop` — or a box's name. Anything after the first word is a note,
# except a `code=XX` word: those two letters, typed alone in KRunner, open
# the entry (the KDOS runner reads this file too).
#
# At every login, before Plasma starts, `kdos-appbox warmup` starts the box
# behind each line, with its bus proxy, so the first launch of the session
# finds it running instead of paying for a cold start. A boxed application's
# launcher id (`app.<id>`, or `app.<id>.<launcher>` for a pack with several)
# names its box; so does a box's name; a host application's id names no box
# and is skipped. At most eight boxes are started, in the order listed, and a
# box that stays idle past its profile's `autostop` is stopped again by
# `kdos-box gc`.
#
# The panel's pinned launchers are Plasma's own (right-click a task, Pin to
# Task Manager) and are not read from here. The shipped list names the apps
# the desks pin, so a fresh account whose pinned app is boxed starts that box
# warm; testing/lnfcheck.py keeps the two in step.
org.kde.konsole code=TE
org.kde.dolphin code=FM
firefox-esr code=FF
org.kde.kate
